hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21582","Affan narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, and Abdullah said: And al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: I stood, I and Ubayy ibn Ka'b, in the shade of the fortress of Hassan. Ubayy said to me: Do you not see people with necks outstretched in seeking the world? He said: I said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Euphrates is about to recede from a mountain of gold. When people hear of it, they hasten to it. Those near it say: By Allah, if we leave people taking of it, they will surely take it all. So people fight until ninety-nine of every hundred are killed. And this is the wording of the hadith of Ubayy from 'Affan."
"21583","Affan narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, and Abdullah said: And al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: I stood, I and Ubayy ibn Ka'b, in the shade of the fortress of Hassan. Ubayy said to me: Do you not see people with necks outstretched in seeking the world? He said: I said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Euphrates is about to recede from a mountain of gold. When people hear of it, they hasten to it. Those near it say: By Allah, if we leave people taking of it, they will surely take it all. So people fight until ninety-nine of every hundred are killed. And this is the wording of the hadith of Ubayy from 'Affan."
"21584","Shuja' ibn Makhlad and Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb said: 'Abdullah ibn Humran al-Humrani narrated to us, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, my father informed me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: I stood, I and Ubayy ibn Ka'b, in the shade of the fortress of Hassan. Ubayy said to me: Do you not see people with necks outstretched in seeking the world? I said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Euphrates is about to recede from a mountain of gold. When people hear of it, they hasten to it. Those near it say: By Allah, if we leave people taking of it, they will surely take it all. So people fight until ninety-nine of every hundred are killed. And this is the wording of the hadith of my father from 'Affan. Abdullah narrated to us, Shuja' ibn Makhlad and Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, they said: 'Abdullah ibn Humran al-Humrani narrated to us, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, my father Ja'far ibn 'Abdullah informed me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Euphrates is about to recede from a mountain of gold, and he mentioned the hadith."
